{"type":"sdk_message","turn":1,"message":{"type":"assistant","parent_tool_use_id":null,"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UXzb3FyNtqbtJayibijNTh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/claude/plan.md << 'EOF'\n# Authentication for To-Do App\n\n## Overview\nAdd user authentication (sign-up and login) to the existing to-do app. Users will need to create an account and log in before accessing their to-do list. Each user's todos will be stored separately.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### 1. HTML Changes (index.html)\n- Add login/signup form section (hidden initially)\n- Add app section (hidden until authenticated)\n- Include fields for email and password\n- Add toggle between login and signup forms\n- Add logout button in app header\n\n### 2. JavaScript Changes (app.js)\n- Implement user authentication system using localStorage\n- Create functions to:\n  - Register new users\n  - Login users\n  - Logout users\n  - Store users and their todos separately by email\n  - Validate credentials\n- Add UI state management (show/hide auth vs app)\n- Modify todo storage to be per-user\n- Add logout functionality\n\n### 3. CSS Changes (style.css)\n- Style authentication forms\n- Add styling for login/signup containers\n- Style user info section with email and logout button\n- Add `.hidden` class for toggling visibility\n- Style form elements and buttons\n\n## Storage Schema\nUsers: JSON object with email as key, hashed password as value\nTodos: Stored under user-specific keys\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Users can sign up with email and password\n- Users can log in with credentials\n- Each user sees only their own todos\n- Logout clears session\n- Simple password validation (non-production, for demo purposes)\nEOF\ncat /tmp/claude/plan.md\n","background":false}}]},"t":24415}
